This directory contains scripts which simulate errors and error
correction for various quantum circuits.  All of these simulations use
the density matrix representation.  Please see our related paper which
can be found at http://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0403114

Scripts
-------

css1.qpro: Encodes a single qubit using the CSS code.  A bit-flip
	   error on the third physical qubit is introduced and
	   detected.

css2.qpro: Encodes a single qubit using the CSS code.  A phase-flip
	   error on the fifth physical qubit is introduced and
	   detected.

css3.qpro: Encodes a single qubit in the state 0.866025|0> + 0.5|1>
	   using the 7-qubit CSS code.  A bit-flip error on the third
	   physical qubit is introduced and detected.

grover_s1.qpro: An implementation of Grover's quantum search algorithm
		for 2 logical data qubits and 1 logical oracle qubit.
		Each logical qubit is encoded with the 7-qubit CSS
		code.  No error is introduced in this circuit.

grover_s_bf1.qpro: An implementation of Grover's quantum search
		   algorithm for 2 logical data qubits and 1 logical
		   oracle qubit.  Each logical qubit is encoded with
		   the 7-qubit CSS code.  A bit-flip error on the
		   third physical qubit of the logical oracle qubit is
		   introduced, detected, and corrected.

grover_s_pf1.qpro: An implementation of Grover's quantum search
		   algorithm for 2 logical data qubits and 1 logical
		   oracle qubit.  Each logical qubit is encoded with
		   the 7-qubit CSS code.  A phase-flip error on the
		   third physical qubit of the logical oracle qubit is
		   introduced, detected, and corrected.
